# Weekly newsletter automation

When researching, writing, or sending the **Sunday weekly newsletter**:

1. Follow **`tools/weekly-newsletter/HOW_TO_ASSEMBLE.md`** (assembly) and **`AGENT_RUNBOOK.md`** (order of operations).
2. Topics: **final expense, whole life, term, IUL, annuities** only. Block Medicare/Medigap.
3. Last **7 days** of reputable news; evergreen if thin; always **3** stories of **equal length**.
4. Follow **`tools/weekly-newsletter/CONTENT_PACKAGE.md`**.
5. 6 a.m. Sunday Chicago send: **julie@ in Spanish**, **admin@ in English**.
6. Do not invent premiums. Do not publish the public blog until Julie asks (`newsletter-consumer-blog` rule).
7. Client letter only. Never: writing-method narration, “a news story does not cancel your policy,” “read every question slowly,” or “we do not have that file / we will not repeat a rate we did not verify.” Julie cut those because they sound weird. Omit unverified numbers silently.
8. After the approved blog and images are live, Facebook is automatic — `tools/weekly-newsletter/FACEBOOK_AUTOMATION.md`. Do not wait for a Tuesday/Thursday prompt.
